WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.866
Mole ran past the rabbit.

2
00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:21.026
The old rabbit fell over.

3
00:00:21.027 --> 00:00:24.238
The other rabbits came out of their holes.

4
00:00:24.239 --> 00:00:27.013
They grumbled at the old rabbit.

5
00:00:27.014 --> 00:00:31.086
"You should have yelled louder!" a gray rabbit said.

6
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:34.896
"You should have been bold!" said a small one.

7
00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:42.028
"You should have told him the rules," said a rabbit with a red ribbon.

8
00:00:42.029 --> 00:00:44.745
But Mole didn't care.

9
00:00:44.746 --> 00:00:48.475
"What a fine day for running!" said Mole.

10
00:00:48.476 --> 00:00:51.205
Suddenly he stopped.

11
00:00:51.206 --> 00:00:53.897
"What's this?" asked Mole.

12
00:00:53.898 --> 00:00:58.815
He saw something new. A river!

13
00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:01.136
He sat on the riverbank.

14
00:01:01.137 --> 00:01:05.633
"The water is so blue!" said Mole.

15
00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:09.868
"How the waves sparkle!"

16
00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.582
Mole looked across the water.

17
00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:15.966
There was a hole in the other riverbank.

18
00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:20.671
"What a cozy place to live!" Mole said.

19
00:01:20.672 --> 00:01:24.280
A small face popped out of the hole.

20
00:01:24.281 --> 00:01:26.169
It was the Water Rat.

21
00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:30.957
"Hello, Mole!" said Water Rat, waving his hand.

22
00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:34.154
"Hello, Rat!" said Mole.

23
00:01:34.155 --> 00:01:37.541
"Would you like to come over?" asked Rat.

24
00:01:37.542 --> 00:01:40.751
"Of course," said Mole happily.

25
00:01:40.752 --> 00:01:44.275
Rat stepped into a little boat by his hole.

26
00:01:44.276 --> 00:01:48.243
He rowed over to Mole.

27
00:01:48.244 --> 00:01:50.633
"Step in!" said Rat.

28
00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:54.753
"This is my first time in a boat!" cried Mole.

29
00:01:54.754 --> 00:01:56.874
Rat was surprised.

30
00:01:56.875 --> 00:02:04.638
"What? Well! Nothing is as great as being in a boat!"
